# Product login for `manualforge capture`.
#
# COPY this file to `.env.capture` in the same folder (the repository root) and
# put the real values there. Copy it — do not rename it — so the template stays
# for the next person.
#
#   cp .env.capture.example .env.capture
#
# `.env.capture` is in .gitignore and can never be committed. THIS file can, so
# never put a real password in it.
#
# A variable already set in the shell wins over this file, so a one-off run
# against another deployment needs no edit here.
#
# Which account: one that can see the screens being photographed. The capture
# only ever reads — it navigates, waits for data and takes a picture.

MANUALFORGE_CAPTURE_USER=
MANUALFORGE_CAPTURE_PASSWORD=
